{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1232758-running-preludes","id":1232758,"title":"Running preludes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-05T17:39:27-07:00","id":1232758,"title":"Running preludes","content":"I really love running preludes in Exalted games. In days gone past this would take the shape of a 2-3 hour solo session with each player, to establish things like their childhood, where they're from, family and rivals, their exaltation of course, and maybe some events that lead them to meeting up with the rest of the group. <br /> <br /> These days me and my group are in our mid to late 30s and we have kids and busy jobs and I'm not sure if I can find the time for this, but I'm worried that it will mean the game will be missing out on a vital first step to have everyone set up right. <br /> <br /> What are your thoughts on preludes? Do you run them? Do you get players to answer FAQs instead? Do you do something else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1229925-hello-i-did-up-a-scavenger-lands-map-based-on-3e\" target=\"_blank\">3e Scavenger Lands map</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/a/NQewCv0\" target=\"_blank\">3e Combat tracker card</a><br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/uGrZk2r\" target=\"_blank\">2e Nexus map</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1079-megapope","name":"Megapope","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T18:41:16-07:00","id":1232765,"title":"","content":"I am gearing up to run a set of preludes for my Hearth of Dynastic scions. All the characters are just graduated from secondary and will be starting their Grand Tour soon, so the prelude will be focused on their graduation and coming out party for their house. <br /> <br /> Typically what I like to use preludes for is to help ease the player into their character\u2019s mindset, as well as plant story points that will come up in like 20-30 sessions. I also don\u2019t do them for 2-3 hours, instead almost all the background stuff has been worked on for the past 2-4 months for my players, so they have most of that kind of prelim work done. Instead, it\u2019s about 30 min of actual \u201cplay time\u201d used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T18:43:59-07:00","id":1232767,"title":"","content":"I love preludes. Had one when I ran Red Keels of Okeanos, basically sat all the players down and dicelessly established how each one got to the Neck, as well as give them reason to be doing stuff there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-05T21:34:49-07:00","id":1232798,"title":"","content":"In my experience my players have had a very negative reaction to running preludes, but my players tend to send 3-8 page backstories for their characters when I tell them I running a new campaign. I think they see me running preludes as me taking control of one of the things they get to have full control over as a player which is the creation of their character and there place in the world. I know some players hate the idea of writing out a backstory but my players seem to enjoy it as a step in character creation. That being said its probably something that is group specific with us, as I've heard a lot of good things from other groups and have had some success with them in other systems, such as Scion/WoD where most of my games had prelude session. <br /> <br /> That being said if I was running a campaign with new players I would probably try to do a prelude session. though not necessary one on one, maybe as a group of one or two separate groups depending on charter relations. Though this is mainly because I feel running Solar characters from session one can be fairly daunting for new players to the system, and I feel I can better ease them into the rules of the system and the lore of the world with them starting as mortals. <i>(Off Topic Thought: Though I've always felt that I would have preferred the core book have character creation for mortals and each Exalted type, including solar, being a separate splat book. Partial for organization and partial to cut down the size of the core, because that book is huge and a bit of a pain to lug around.)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23987-chellgame","name":"Chellgame","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}